<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the status is not equal to 0, a message fires until the status is equal to 0.  The program copies each channel's Command 48 data (24 bytes) into a (224 boolean array).  You can read the boolean array based on byte-bit pattern from 0 -23 bytes and 0-8 bits.  ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch0.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch1.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch2.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch3.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch4.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch5.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch6.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ,NEQ(Ref_Inp.Ch7.DeviceStatus.FieldDeviceStatus,0) ]OTE(Sts_DiagInfoAvail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the HART status is Good from the previous rung, then this logic is skipped skpped to the rung containing the function LBL <EndofLoop>.  200 is moved into Val_ExtSts 1-3. 
If the HART status is not is Good, the HART_DiagData.[0-24 sints] is checked at each bit to see whether or not the bits are true. The first bit of the array is initially checked at sint 0 bit 1 and continues until the first 3 indexed bits [0-199] are collected and put into the prioritized Val_ExtSts 1-3.  

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_DiagInfoAvail) ,XIC(Wrk_DiagMSGT.TT) ]XIO(Wrk_DiagMSGT.DN)MOV(5000,Wrk_DiagMSGT.PRE)TON(Wrk_DiagMSGT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
